cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package or its datasets, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "timss-math: Released TIMSS mathematics items with IRT parameters, for predicting item parameters and testing LLMs"
abstract: >-
  Item-level datasets built from every TIMSS released mathematics set
  (1995 to 2011, grades 4 and 8, and TIMSS Advanced), with the official IRT
  item parameters and the TIMSS reporting-scale constants attached, and two
  uses of them: predictions of the IRT parameters of new items by an LLM or
  by Jev, grounded in the most similar calibrated items; and LLMs taking the
  released items as a test, as test takers (a benchmark) or as students
  (synthetic participants), scored with the IRT models on each calibration's
  scale and on the TIMSS reporting scale.
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Ze
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wang-ze/timss-ai"
keywords:
  - TIMSS
  - mathematics assessment
  - item response theory
  - item parameter prediction
  - large language models
  - LLM evaluation
  - benchmark
  - synthetic data
  - TIMSS reporting scale
  - Jev
  - retrieval-augmented generation
